# FlowDocs Design System

Dark-theme, dense, developer-tool aesthetic (similar to Linear / Vercel
dashboard / n8n). Prioritize information density and clarity over decoration.

## Colors

- Background (app shell): `#0d0f14`
- Panel / card background: `#151822`
- Sidebar background: `#12141a` (slightly darker than cards)
- Border / divider: `#23262f` (thin, 1px, subtle — never heavy shadows)
- Primary text: `#e5e7eb`
- Secondary/muted text: `#9ca3af`
- Accent (primary actions, active nav item, selected node, links):
  `#3b82f6`
- Accent hover: `#2563eb`

### Status colors (used consistently across nodes, badges, logs)
- Success: `#22c55e` (green)
- Running / in-progress: `#3b82f6` (blue)
- Idle / waiting: `#9ca3af` (gray)
- Warning: `#f59e0b` (amber)
- Error: `#ef4444` (red)

### Category accent colors (node left-border / icon color on canvas)
- Preprocessing: cyan/teal
- OCR: orange
- RAG / Embeddings: purple
- Extraction: pink/magenta
- Export / Output: yellow
- Logic / Conditions: blue

## Layout

- **Left sidebar**: fixed width (~200-220px), icon + label nav items,
  logo/app name at top, "+ New Workflow" primary button below logo,
  user avatar + name pinned to bottom.
- **Top bar**: breadcrumb-style navigation (e.g. "Workflows > Invoice
  Processing Pipeline"), with contextual actions on the right (Share,
  Versions, Run Workflow button in accent blue).
- **Dashboard**: stat cards in a 4-column grid up top (icon, label, big
  number, small trend indicator), followed by a card grid of items
  (workflows/documents) below, each card showing status badge, metadata
  (node count, run count, last run time).
- **Node canvas editor**: infinite canvas with draggable nodes connected by
  curved bezier edges; left palette panel (searchable, grouped by category,
  collapsible sections); right inspector panel appears when a node is
  selected, with tabs (Parameters / I-O / Test); zoom controls bottom-left;
  minimap bottom-right.
- **Execution view**: same canvas layout but read-only, with a right-side
  live log panel (timestamped, color-coded by level: info/warn/error) and a
  top progress bar showing overall run completion.

## Typography

- Base font size: 13-14px (dense, not spacious)
- Font weight: medium (500) for labels/headers, regular (400) for body/logs
- Headers use a slightly larger size (15-16px) with lighter weight, muted
  color (e.g. page titles like "Dashboard" appear in muted gray, not white)

## Components

- Cards: `rounded-lg` (8px), subtle 1px border, no heavy box-shadow, slight
  background lift from the page background
- Buttons: primary = accent blue background, white text, `rounded-md`;
  secondary = transparent/outline with border
- Badges/status pills: small, `rounded-full`, colored dot + label, colored
  text matching status color at reduced opacity background
- Node cards on canvas: `rounded-md`, colored left border (2-3px) by
  category, icon + node name + node type subtitle + status dot
- Inputs/dropdowns: dark background (`#0d0f14` or `#151822`), thin border,
  focus state uses accent blue border/ring

## Non-negotiables

- Never use light backgrounds or light-mode colors anywhere.
- Never use heavy drop-shadows — depth comes from subtle border + background
  contrast only.
- Keep spacing tight and information-dense; do not add generous whitespace
  that would look like a marketing site rather than a dev tool.
